Z||000015||Songman||08-28-2001||09:13 PM||||It used to The Nashville Network for 25 years. Turner had nothing to do with it.. and they had ratings... some of the longest running shows on TV. But at the same time the Gaylords put Opryland on the chopping block and built a mall they also sold TNN. In this case it is not about ratings it is about greed...<P>And yes, they will drop Dukes of Hazzard. The latest show on the chopping block was the Grand Ole Opry. And we know that nobody would want to see that! It's only been around since 1912 and going stronger than ever! Luckily CMT picked it up...<P>TNN is now nothing but a clone of all the other so-called 'cool' channels. Kinda sad that they are just copying everyone else's shows. And they had to make sure and get away from country so there slogan was 'We got POP!' How ridiculous is that?<P>Maybe it's just me but I hate sell outs. I remember when all the pop singers came over to country because it was selling better... Now 10 years later all they have accomplished is watering down country music so it sounds pop.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
